Package: raye-taskmanager
Architecture: any
Depends: raye-style, qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-controls,
         qml6-module-qtquick-layouts, qml6-module-qtquick-window,
         qml6-module-qtcore, qml6-module-org-kde-kirigami,
         ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: pkexec, pci.ids, kde-cli-tools
Description: Raye Linux Task Manager
 See what the machine is doing and take a hand in it: the apps and
 background processes with their processor, memory and disk use, live
 graphs of the processor, memory, disks, network and graphics card, the
 apps that start at sign-in, the people signed in, every process with its
 priority, and the system's services. End a program that has stopped
 answering, or hold one back so the rest of the machine keeps up.

Package: raye-calendar
Architecture: any
Depends: raye-style, qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-controls,
         qml6-module-qtquick-layouts, qml6-module-qtquick-window,
         qml6-module-qtquick-templates, qml6-module-qtquick-dialogs,
         qml6-module-qtcore, systemd, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Raye Linux Calendar
 Note the dates that matter, birthdays, appointments and trips, and get a
 reminder on time, with Later and Dismiss. Day, week, month and agenda
 views, simple repeats, colours, public holidays if wanted, and .ics
 import and export. The events stay in one file on this computer, and
 nothing runs in the background between two reminders.

Package: raye-clock
Architecture: any
Depends: raye-style, qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-controls,
         qml6-module-qtquick-layouts, qml6-module-qtquick-window,
         qml6-module-qtquick-templates, qml6-module-qtquick-shapes,
         qml6-module-qtmultimedia, qml6-module-qtcore, systemd, pkexec, polkitd,
         ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Raye Linux Clock
 Alarms that ring at the time you set, once or on chosen days, with a
 name, a sound and Snooze, even when the window is closed. Timers, as
 many as you like, side by side; a stopwatch with laps; and the time in
 the cities that matter to you. A sleeping PC wakes up for an alarm
 when its clock can do it. Nothing runs in the background between two
 alarms.

Package: raye-graphics
Architecture: any
Depends: raye-style, pkexec, polkitd, systemd,
         qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-controls,
         qml6-module-qtquick-layouts, qml6-module-qtquick-window,
         qml6-module-qtquick-templates, qml6-module-qtcore,
         qml6-module-org-kde-kirigami,
         ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: pci.ids
Description: Raye Linux graphics card panel
 Watch the graphics card live: how busy it is, its clock speed, video
 memory, temperature, power and fan. On an AMD Radeon card, choose its
 performance mode and workload profile, its power limit and a fan
 curve, within the limits the card itself gives; the settings come back
 at each start, and Restore defaults hands the card back its own. An
 NVIDIA card shows its readings and opens the NVIDIA Control Panel.

Package: xdg-desktop-portal-raye
Architecture: any
Depends: raye-style, xdg-desktop-portal, xdg-desktop-portal-kde,
         qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-controls,
         qml6-module-qtquick-layouts, qml6-module-qtquick-window,
         ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: pipewire
Description: Raye Linux screen sharing
 Lets apps share your screen or a window, after you choose what to
 share, and shows while something is shared so you can stop it. Other
 requests of apps keep the desktop's usual handling.

Package: raye-app-identity
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Raye Linux names and icons for the stock apps
 Gives the apps that come with Raye plain names and matching icons in
 Start, search and Open with: Terminal, Calculator, Photos, Music. It
 also keeps technical tools out of Start. Package updates cannot undo
 this, and removing the package brings the usual names back.

Package: raye-controlpanel
Architecture: any
Depends: raye-settings, raye-style,
         qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-controls,
         qml6-module-qtquick-layouts, qml6-module-qtquick-window,
         qml6-module-qtcore, qml6-module-org-kde-kirigami,
         ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: raye-taskmanager, raye-regedit
Description: Raye Linux Control Panel
 Every setting of the PC by category, or as one list of large or small
 icons, the way the classic Control Panel shows them: Programs and
 Features, User Accounts, Network and Sharing Centre, Sound, Power
 Options, Devices and Printers, Fonts and the rest. Each one opens its
 page in Raye Settings. System Tools gathers the Task Manager, the
 Registry Editor and the other tools for people who look after the PC.

Package: raye-regedit
Architecture: any
Depends: raye-style, dconf-service, pkexec,
         qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-controls,
         qml6-module-qtquick-layouts, qml6-module-qtquick-window,
         qml6-module-qtquick-dialogs, qml6-module-qtqml-models,
         qml6-module-qtcore,
         ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Raye Linux Registry Editor
 Shows the settings files of the apps and of the system as one tree of
 keys and values, as the Registry Editor does: the user's files in
 ~/.config, the desktop database (dconf), the defaults in /etc/xdg and
 a chosen list of system files. Values can be changed, added, deleted,
 searched, exported and imported. Each change touches only the line of
 its value, keeps a copy of the file first and can be undone; system
 files need root access.
